WEBVTT

00:00:30.034 --> 00:00:31.557
Merlin's beard.

00:00:32.689 --> 00:00:35.082
No need to disfigure me,
Albus.

00:00:35.126 --> 00:00:39.783
Well, I must say you make a very
convincing armchair, Horace.

00:00:39.826 --> 00:00:41.611
It's all in the upholstery.

00:00:41.654 --> 00:00:44.483
I come by the stuffing
naturally. What gave me away?

00:00:44.527 --> 00:00:46.006
Dragon's blood.

00:00:47.486 --> 00:00:48.922
Oh.

00:00:48.966 --> 00:00:50.707
DUMBLEDORE:
Oh, yes, introductions.

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:54.362
Harry, I'd like you to meet an
old friend and colleague of mine

00:00:54.406 --> 00:00:56.364
Horace Slughorn.

00:00:56.408 --> 00:00:58.062
Horace,

00:00:58.105 --> 00:01:01.239
well, you know
who this is.

00:01:01.282 --> 00:01:03.459
SLUGHORN:
Harry Potter.

00:01:03.502 --> 00:01:06.287
[CHUCKLES]

00:01:06.331 --> 00:01:08.594
DUMBLEDORE:
What's with all the theatrics,
Horace?

00:01:08.638 --> 00:01:11.118
You weren't, by any chance,
waiting for someone else?

00:01:11.162 --> 00:01:14.121
Someone else? I'm sure
I don't know what you mean.

00:01:14.165 --> 00:01:16.080
All right,
the Death Eaters have been

00:01:16.123 --> 00:01:17.777
trying to recruit me
for over a year.

00:01:17.821 --> 00:01:19.170
Do you know what that's like?

00:01:19.213 --> 00:01:20.911
You can only say no
so many times,

00:01:20.954 --> 00:01:23.130
so I never stay anywhere
more than a week.

00:01:23.174 --> 00:01:25.698
Muggles who own this place
are in the Canary Islands.

00:01:25.742 --> 00:01:27.308
Well, I think
we should put it back

00:01:27.352 --> 00:01:30.616
in order for them,
don't you? Mind.

00:01:43.411 --> 00:01:45.370
[PIANO KEYS CLINKING]

00:01:45.413 --> 00:01:47.415
[♪♪♪]

00:01:54.901 --> 00:01:57.338
[SQUEAKING]

00:02:05.346 --> 00:02:08.088
That was fun.

00:02:08.132 --> 00:02:11.004
Do you mind if I use the loo?No, of course.

00:02:12.484 --> 00:02:15.182
Don't think I don't know
why you're here, Albus.

00:02:15.226 --> 00:02:16.444
The answer's still no.

00:02:16.488 --> 00:02:20.753
Absolutely
and unequivocally, no.

00:02:29.196 --> 00:02:32.373
You're very like your father.

00:02:32.417 --> 00:02:34.114
Except for the eyes.
You have your--

00:02:34.158 --> 00:02:35.942
My mother's eyes. Yeah.

00:02:35.986 --> 00:02:39.250
Lily. Lovely Lily. She was
exceedingly bright, your mother.

00:02:39.293 --> 00:02:42.645
Even more impressive when one
considers she was Muggle-born.

00:02:42.688 --> 00:02:45.561
One of my best friends is
Muggle-born. Best in our year.

00:02:45.604 --> 00:02:47.606
Please don't think
I'm prejudiced. No, no.

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:50.870
Your mother was one
of my absolute favorites.

00:02:50.914 --> 00:02:52.045
Look, there she is.

00:02:52.089 --> 00:02:53.917
Right at the front.

00:03:02.447 --> 00:03:05.450
All mine.
Each and every one.

00:03:05.493 --> 00:03:07.626
Ex-students, I mean.

00:03:09.933 --> 00:03:13.501
You recognize Barnabas Cuffe,
editor of The Daily Prophet.

00:03:14.764 --> 00:03:16.983
Always takes my owl,
should I wish to register

00:03:17.027 --> 00:03:19.943
an opinion on the news
of the day.

00:03:19.986 --> 00:03:22.989
Gwenog Jones,
captain of the Holyhead Harpies.

00:03:23.033 --> 00:03:25.818
Free tickets
whenever I want them.

00:03:25.862 --> 00:03:28.778
Of course, I haven't been
to a match in some time.

00:03:30.475 --> 00:03:31.650
Ah, yes.

00:03:31.694 --> 00:03:34.174
Regulus Black.

00:03:34.218 --> 00:03:36.220
You no doubt know
of his older brother Sirius.

00:03:36.263 --> 00:03:38.614
Died a few weeks ago.

00:03:38.657 --> 00:03:41.312
I taught the whole Black family,
except Sirius.

00:03:41.355 --> 00:03:43.706
It's a shame. Talented boy.

00:03:43.749 --> 00:03:46.230
I got Regulus
when he came along, of course,

00:03:46.273 --> 00:03:49.886
but I'd have liked the set.

00:03:49.929 --> 00:03:51.148
DUMBLEDORE:
Horace?

00:03:51.191 --> 00:03:53.454
Do you mind if I take this?

00:03:57.807 --> 00:04:00.026
I do love knitting patterns.

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:01.767
Yes, of course.
But you're not leaving?

00:04:01.811 --> 00:04:05.031
Oh, I think I know a lost cause
when I see one. Regrettable.

00:04:05.075 --> 00:04:07.381
I would have considered it
a great personal triumph

00:04:07.425 --> 00:04:10.515
had you consented to return
to Hogwarts. Oh, well.

00:04:10.558 --> 00:04:14.258
You're like my friend
Mr. Potter here, one of a kind.

00:04:14.301 --> 00:04:16.956
Well, bye-bye, Horace.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.349
Bye.

00:04:29.055 --> 00:04:31.754
All right. I'll do it.

00:04:31.797 --> 00:04:34.147
But I want Professor
Merrythought's old office,

00:04:34.191 --> 00:04:36.715
not the water closet
I had before.

00:04:36.759 --> 00:04:38.021
And I expect a raise.

00:04:38.064 --> 00:04:40.980
These are mad times
we live in. Mad.

00:04:42.678 --> 00:04:44.505
They are indeed.

00:04:44.549 --> 00:04:46.333
[DUMBLEDORE HUMMING]

00:04:47.683 --> 00:04:49.728
HARRY:
Sir, exactly what was
all that about?

00:04:49.772 --> 00:04:52.818
You are talented,
famous and powerful.

00:04:52.862 --> 00:04:55.081
Everything Horace values.

00:04:55.125 --> 00:04:58.694
Professor Slughorn is gonna try
to collect you, Harry.

00:04:58.737 --> 00:05:01.174
You would be
his crowning jewel.

00:05:01.218 --> 00:05:03.437
That's why he's returning
to Hogwarts.

00:05:03.481 --> 00:05:07.485
And it's crucial
he should return.

00:05:07.528 --> 00:05:10.706
I fear I may have stolen a
wondrous night from you, Harry.

00:05:10.749 --> 00:05:12.664
She was, truthfully,

00:05:12.708 --> 00:05:15.885
very pretty, the girl.

00:05:15.928 --> 00:05:17.321
It's all right, sir.

00:05:17.364 --> 00:05:19.540
I'll go back tomorrow,
make some excuse.

00:05:19.584 --> 00:05:20.846
Oh, you'll not be returning

00:05:20.890 --> 00:05:23.414
to Little Whinging tonight,
Harry.

00:05:23.457 --> 00:05:26.591
But, sir, what about Hedwig?
And my trunk?

00:05:26.634 --> 00:05:29.289
Both are waiting for you.

00:05:36.949 --> 00:05:38.255
[WATER SPLASHES]

00:05:38.298 --> 00:05:39.952
[HARRY GRUNTS]

00:05:43.477 --> 00:05:44.957
[GROANS]

00:05:47.525 --> 00:05:49.527
[♪♪♪]

00:05:59.232 --> 00:06:01.539
[HEDWIG CHIRPS]

00:06:02.801 --> 00:06:04.368
Hedwig.

00:06:06.936 --> 00:06:08.154
Mum?

00:06:09.503 --> 00:06:10.940
Ginny, what is it?

00:06:10.983 --> 00:06:13.594
I was only wondering
when Harry got here.

00:06:13.638 --> 00:06:17.163
What? Harry? Harry who?Harry Potter, of course.

00:06:17.207 --> 00:06:20.427
I think I'd know if Harry Potter
was in my house, wouldn't I?

00:06:20.471 --> 00:06:22.821
His trunk's in the kitchen,
and his owl.

00:06:22.865 --> 00:06:24.301
No, dear,
I seriously doubt that.

00:06:24.344 --> 00:06:25.432
[HEDWIG CHIRPING]

00:06:25.476 --> 00:06:26.694
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

00:06:26.738 --> 00:06:28.435
RON:
Harry? Did someone say "Harry"?

00:06:28.479 --> 00:06:30.611
GINNY:
Me, nosy. Is he up there
with you?

00:06:30.655 --> 00:06:32.309
Of course not.
I'd know if my best friend

00:06:32.352 --> 00:06:33.571
was in my room, wouldn't I?

00:06:33.614 --> 00:06:34.920
HERMIONE:
Is that an owl?

00:06:34.964 --> 00:06:36.400
GINNY:
You haven't seen him, have you?

00:06:36.443 --> 00:06:38.402
He's wandering about the house.

00:06:38.445 --> 00:06:40.186
HERMIONE: Really?RON: Really.

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:41.971
MOLLY:
Harry!

